---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base title="About" description="About Kunal Mathur — embedded systems and IoT engineer in Bangalore.">
  <article>
    <header class="post-header about-header">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <img
        class="avatar"
        src={`${base}/profile.jpg`}
        alt="Portrait of Kunal Mathur"
        width="301"
        height="330"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I'm Kunal Mathur, a software engineer focused on architecting and delivering
        scalable IoT products and embedded platforms that evolve with growing business
        and technical requirements. I specialize in C++ development, Embedded Linux,
        and Yocto-based platform engineering.
      </p>
      <p>
        My passion centers on the intersection of hardware and software — building
        systems that bridge the physical and digital worlds. I've developed expertise
        in taking embedded platforms from prototype to production, always with an eye
        toward maintainability and future growth.
      </p>
      <p>
        Currently I'm a software engineer at <strong>Teledyne Isco</strong>, where I
        develop Yocto images and drive migration projects that move products from
        off-the-shelf Linux distributions onto Yocto-based platforms — bringing
        reproducible builds and long-term maintainability to instrumentation that
        has to run reliably in the field.
      </p>
      <p>
        Previously, at <strong>Sensormatic (Johnson Controls)</strong>, I architected
        codebases spanning multiple product lines and led a team of engineers through
        complex technical challenges while keeping a strong product focus. I studied
        Electronics and Communication Engineering at The LNM Institute of Information
        Technology.
      </p>

      <h2>What I work with</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Languages</strong> — C++, C, Python, Bash</li>
        <li><strong>Platforms</strong> — Embedded Linux, Yocto, systemd, ARM &amp; edge devices</li>
        <li><strong>Tooling</strong> — CMake, BitBake, GCC, GDB, Docker, OTA update systems</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Specialties</strong> — IoT platform architecture, embedded Linux
          distribution engineering, cross-product codebase design, remote device
          management &amp; observability
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>This site</h2>
      <p>
        I write about embedded systems, development tools, gadgets, and whatever tech
        currently has my attention. Everything here is my own opinion, written by me.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        I love connecting with fellow engineers to talk embedded systems, IoT
        architecture, and platform engineering. Reach me by
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>email</a>, or find me on
        <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a> and <a href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.
        I typically reply within a day or two.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
